  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'If the pot is empty all players ante. Dealer deals two cards face down to each player. Players declare in (compete for the pot) or out (drop out; no extra loss). Each player who declared in receives one more card face down. If more than one stayed in, they show hands and the best three-card hand wins the pot. All players who stayed in but did not win each pay an amount equal to the whole pot into the next deal. If only one stays in, that player takes the pot without showing.',
    Player: 'If the pot is empty all players ante. Dealer deals two cards face down to each player. Players declare in (compete for the pot) or out (drop out; no extra loss). Each player who declared in receives one more card face down. If more than one stayed in, they show hands and the best three-card hand wins the pot. All players who stayed in but did not win each pay an amount equal to the whole pot into the next deal. If only one stays in, that player takes the pot without showing.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the best three-card hand among players who declare in, or be the only player to declare in.',
    gameplay: 'If the pot is empty all players ante. Dealer deals two cards face down to each player. Players declare in (compete for the pot) or out (drop out; no extra loss). Each player who declared in receives one more card face down. If more than one stayed in, they show hands and the best three-card hand wins the pot. All players who stayed in but did not win each pay an amount equal to the whole pot into the next deal. If only one stays in, that player takes the pot without showing.',
    keyRules: [
      'Two cards each face down; declare in or out (turn or simultaneous e.g. chips in fist); one card dealt to each player who is in; three-card Guts ranking: three of a kind, straight flush, straight, flush, pair, nothing; losers who stayed in each match the pot; agree ante and optional max loss per deal before play.',
